City Council on July 29 and 30, 2026, adopted the following:

1. City Council authorize the General Manager, Transportation Services to negotiate, enter into and execute a license agreement with North Drive Investments Inc to permit temporary construction access across the reserve running along Post Road for the limited purpose of accessing the rear of the lands municipally known as 8 and 10 Hyde Park Circle via Post Road, all in a form satisfactory to the City Solicitor.

2. City Council direct the General Manager, Transportations Services to include in any license agreement entered into further to Part 1 above the following conditions:

a. the proposed access be consistent with all approved development agreements and any conditions imposed by the City through the development approval process;

b. the proposed access does not adversely impact utilities, existing easements or similar land interests, grading and drainage conditions, trees or other City interests or infrastructure;

c. the proposed access be temporary and limited in scope and duration to only that which is strictly necessary to facilitate construction access;

d. the applicant agrees to restore all affected City lands at the applicant’s sole cost and expense, to the City’s satisfaction;

e. the applicant provides a financial security to the City in a form and amount fixed by the General Manager, Transportation Services to secure the applicant’s obligations under the agreement;

f. the applicant indemnify and save harmless the City from and against all claims, demands, actions, losses, costs, damages, and expenses arising from or related to the exercise of the rights granted under the license agreement, including any environmental contamination, discharge, release, or otherwise, and maintain insurance in the types and amounts satisfactory to the General Manager, Transportation Services;

g. the applicant pay the City any fees otherwise payable, including but not limited to fees payable under Toronto Municipal Code Chapter 441, Fees and Charges, for construction access permits; and

h. the applicant accept other additional or amended conditions as the City Solicitor or the General Manger, Transportation Services, deems appropriate to protect the interests of the City.

3. City Council further request the General Manager, Transportation Services to continue addressing construction-related compliance and neighbourhood impacts on Hyde Park Circle through the applicable permit, inspection and enforcement processes while the temporary-access review is underway.
